Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:01:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(storage): fail-closed reclaim and reservation
 compensation

Context:
Promotion PR #100 Greptile P1s on exported 0002: a reservation PUT can strand the name if the following body PUT misses, and a KV miss for legacy R2 objects without custom expiration metadata was treated as proof of expiry.

Expected behavior:
If identical-body reclaim wins a reservation but the body PUT returns null or throws, expire that reservation generation-safely and return null. Legacy objects without R2 expiry metadata are reclaimed only when KV metadata is present and expired; a KV miss is fail-closed and does not overwrite a live object.

Acceptance criteria:
- body PUT miss after reservation leaves the name retryable without clobbering a newer generation
- live legacy R2 plus KV miss is not reclaimed
- expired legacy R2 with present expired KV metadata remains reclaimable

Constraints:
- generic upstream behavior only
- no Durable Object, lease framework, or orphan sweeper
- do not rewrite source PR #99 HEAD a3482e05a7ddf808a48ffe2f9e0ebafc758f7e26
- remaining KV+cleanup double-failure residual stays ACCEPTED_RESIDUAL_RISK

Validation:
- RED: writeConcurrency.spec.ts 2 failed (legacy KV miss reclaimed; reservation retry null)
- GREEN: Node 22 pnpm exec vitest run worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts -> 9 passed
- REGRESSION: Node 22 pnpm exec vitest run -> 23 files, 187 tests passed
- prettier --check, eslint, tsc --noEmit PASS

